# Files where a change quietly weakens a gate rather than obviously breaking
# something. Everything here needs a human to look at it.
#
# The risk is not that someone edits these carelessly. It is that loosening a
# rule looks exactly like fixing a failure, and a board that passes because the
# check was widened looks identical to one that passes because it is correct.

# The fab limits and the boards' own design rules. Widening a clearance or a
# track width makes DRC pass without changing the board.
/hw/fab/                @prizos
/hw/**/rules.kicad_dru  @prizos

# The design checks, and the guard that counts them.
/hw/checks/             @prizos

# What the simulation is allowed to come out as. Moving a band is the same
# thing as deciding the circuit is fine after all.
/hw/**/sim/limits.py    @prizos

# The models the simulation rests on. A fitted model is an assumption, and
# changing one changes every number downstream of it.
/hw/**/sim/models/      @prizos

# The tooling the gates run through.
/hw/tools/              @prizos
/.github/workflows/     @prizos
